# Build context exclusions, shared by every image built from this repo.
#
# Docker uploads the entire context to the daemon before the first instruction
# runs, so this file is both a speed control and a correctness one. A host
# `node_modules` that leaked in would shadow the one the build installs and
# would carry the host's platform-specific binaries — a glibc SWC build landing
# in a musl image, for instance, which fails at runtime rather than at build.
#
# Scoped by pattern rather than by app, so adding `apps/api/Dockerfile` needs no
# change here.

# Dependency trees and build output. Always produced inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/build
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/api/bin

# Git metadata and CI config. Nothing in any build step reads them, and `.git`
# in particular is large and changes on every commit, so including it would
# invalidate the context on every build.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Agent worktrees nested inside the repo (see .gitignore). Each is a full
# working copy — including its own node_modules — so leaving this out makes the
# context grow by a whole repo per concurrent agent.
.claude

# Local environment and secrets. `.env.example` is committed and harmless, but
# there is no reason for any of it to be in an image, so the whole family goes.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Terraform state and variable files. State contains resource identifiers and
# occasionally secrets; neither belongs anywhere near a build context.
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
!**/*.tfvars.example

# Infrastructure and prose. Not inputs to any application build.
infra
docs
**/*.md

# Editor and OS cruft.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/*.pem

# One exception, and it is narrow on purpose. The blanket `**/*.pem` above is a
# safety rule about private keys, and it stays: a key that reaches a build
# context reaches a layer, and a layer is forever. This file is the opposite
# kind of PEM — 108 Amazon RDS *public* root certificates, published by AWS at a
# URL with no authentication, which apps/api's image needs in order to make
# POSTGRES_SSLMODE=verify-full mean anything (see apps/api/certs/README.md).
#
# Named by exact directory rather than by a pattern like `!**/certs/*.pem`, so
# that a future `certs/` somewhere else does not inherit the exemption silently.
# Order matters here: the last matching pattern wins, so this must stay below.
!apps/api/certs/*.pem
